# 15. DATA RECOVERY AND FAILURE HANDLING

A classroom scoring session must not lose data because of a temporary network interruption.

Implement:
- Explicit save confirmation.
- Draft persistence.
- Retry mechanisms.
- Idempotent writes.
- Server-authoritative score retrieval.
- Conflict detection.
- Recovery after browser refresh.
- Recovery after reconnect.
- Clear error messages.
- Backup and restoration strategy appropriate to the selected infrastructure.

Do not silently discard conflicting edits.

If two authorized graders modify the same assessment revision, detect the conflict and resolve it according to the configured ownership policy.

If a request times out, determine whether the original operation succeeded before attempting a new submission.

The user must always know whether their data was saved.

